      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOMORENIGHTSHIFT (1) has been thereabouts without cracking the top 3 for some time, and he has been in work for some time, but he looks to have found the right race here, and 1 of his 4 career wins has come on this track. The blinkers go back on, and he would not be a shock winner. DELRICO (3) weakened in the run home after hitting the front early on in the home straight at Tamworth a week ago, and that effort should have him spot on for this easier assignment. Nick Heywood picks up the ride, and he could coax that little bit extra out of this gelding where it matters most. YES SIREE (2) has been looking for 1600m, and he was only 2 lengths from the winner in provincial company 2 weeks ago at Hawkesbury. He maps to receive the run of the race from the pole position, and is worth each-way consideration. NAVAL OFFICER (7) raced greenly when making his run last start. Stick with him.",
